I have a 53C895 in my PWS, running Norbert's 2.6.8, no problem.

The problem is that ext3 doesn't work because of a compiler bug in gcc-3.3 
(#261893)

Loading the ext3 module causes a kernel OOPS, after which the module is 
still loaded, but ext3 is obviously not supported.

I have only XFS on my PWS, so I don't see the problem, as long as I force 
ext3 out of the initrd. The reason is that, instead of looking in /etc/fstab 
for the fstypes of  the various partitions, the initrd tries just any 
supported fstype in alphabetical order. since ext3 is before xfs, I was 
still seeing OOPSes, even though I'm not using ext3 anywhere.

Jan-Jaap

